<LanguageData>
  <!--EN: A resilient relic from the spacer astronaut era. Offers unmatched insulation and near total fire resistance, safeguarding wearers from environmental hazards in space. Its outdated design significantly hampers movement, making wearers slow and less agile. Despite its minimal armor capabilities, its historical significance as a piece of early space exploration history remains undiminished.-->
  <VRE_AncientAstrosuit.description>源自大航天时代的老古董。这种装备具有无可比拟的隔温与防火效果，能支持穿戴者在环境恶劣的太空中活动。虽然其落后的笨重设计会显著降低移动速度与灵活性，防护能力也并不出色，不过作为人类早期太空探索历史的智慧结晶之一，它仍然有着不可估量的历史意义。</VRE_AncientAstrosuit.description>
  <!--EN: ancient astrosuit-->
  <VRE_AncientAstrosuit.label>远古宇航服</VRE_AncientAstrosuit.label>
  <!--EN: rotblood-->
  <VRE_Filth_RotBlood.label>腐臭血液</VRE_Filth_RotBlood.label>
  <!--EN: An ancient ship part, torn off of an old space exploration craft, mostly destroyed on reentry. It might be thousands of years old.\n\nThis one may contain one or more of the remaining space crew. Governments used to send out crafts filled with immortal fungoids, wicked, twisted experimental xenotypes that can survive the centuries-long space journeys. The fungoids onboard have most likely lost their sense of self long ago. They must have been stuck in this space craft module for hundreds of years.-->
  <VRE_FungoidShipPart.description>一块古老的飞船残骸，可能有数千年的历史了。它曾是某艘太空探索飞船的一部分，而其他船体则早已在重返大气层时烧毁殆尽了。\n\n残骸内可能装有数名已变成菌尸种的船员，这些样貌扭曲骇人的不死异种能在长达数世纪的太空旅行中存活下来。由于被困在里面太久，他们或许早就失去了理智与思考能力。</VRE_FungoidShipPart.description>
  <!--EN: ship part (fungoid)-->
  <VRE_FungoidShipPart.label>飞船部件（菌尸种）</VRE_FungoidShipPart.label>
</LanguageData>
